            "id": "4674422",
            "title": "Nvidia declines, adding to evidence of an AI bubble destined to pop, says SA analyst",
            "description": "<html><body><p class=\"MsoNormal\" data-eci=\"true\">Nvidia (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NVDA\" title=\"NVIDIA Corporation\">NVDA</a></span></span>) ended -2.9% on Wednesday despite reporting revenue and profits that exceeded analyst expectations, as Seeking Alpha analyst <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/author/daniel-jones#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link%7Cfirst_level_url%3Anews\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Daniel Jones\">Daniel Jones</a> warned that \"evidence is continuing to grow that we are truly in an AI bubble that is destined to pop.\"</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The benchmark S&amp;P 500 (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500#source=section%3Amain_content%7Cbutton%3Abody_link%7Cfirst_level_url%3Anews\" title=\"S&amp;P 500 Index\">SP500</a>) finished -0.2%, while the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/COMP:IND\" title=\"NASDAQ Composite Index\">COMP:IND</a></span></span>) ended +0.4, and the blue-chip Dow (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/DJI\" title=\"Dow Jones Industrial Average Index\">DJI</a></span></span>) finished -1.1%.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Nvidia’s (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NVDA\" title=\"NVIDIA Corporation\">NVDA</a>) almost 30% decline over the past month is adding to worries within the technology space, Jones said.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">In addition, the Federal Reserve released its October meeting minutes, with the central bank warning that artificial intelligence acts as \"a driver of both inflation and potential financial instability.”.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The Fed also warned that future interest rate hikes would very likely occur.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Investors are assigning almost a 92% chance that the Federal Reserve will hike interest rates by 25 basis points, according to the CME FedWatch Tool.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">While central bank reports project inflation could fall sharply in upcoming years, Jones noted this would likely come at a cost.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">\"I actually think that is likely to occur, though I expect it to be as part of the fallout involving a stagflationary recession,\" the analyst said.</p>\n</body></html>",
            "image": "https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2249691593/image_2249691593.jpg?io=getty-c-w630",
            "link": "https://seekingalpha.com/news/4674422-nvidia-declines-adding-to-evidence-of-an-ai-bubble-destined-to-pop-says-sa-analyst",
            "pub_date": "2026-11-19 05:33:52",
            "source": "seekalpha",
            "kind": 1,
            "language": "en"
        },
        {
            "id": "4674421",
            "title": "Yelp announces workforce reduction affecting nearly 5% of employees",
            "description": "<html><body><ul>\n<li>Yelp (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/YELP\" title=\"Yelp Inc.\">YELP</a></span></span>) <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/filing/310316250\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"announced\">announced</a> a workforce reduction on November 18, 2026, expected to affect nearly 5% of its full-time employees.</li>\n<li>The company plans to reinvest the substantial majority of resulting cost savings into its business, focusing on high-return growth opportunities, particularly AI-powered offerings.</li>\n<li>Yelp expects restructuring charges of ~$14M–$16M, primarily in Q4 2026 and Q1 2027.</li>\n<li>The charges will include severance payments and related employee benefit costs and are expected to reduce net income but not adjusted EBITDA.</li>\n<li>The company maintained its FY2026 revenue guidance of $1.455B–$1.460B.</li>\n<li>FY2026 adjusted EBITDA guidance remains unchanged at $320M–$325M.</li>\n<li>Yelp intends to exclude workforce reduction-related charges from its non-GAAP financial measures, including adjusted EBITDA.</li>\n</ul>\n</body></html>",
            "image": "https://static.seekingalpha.com/assets/og_image_1200-29b2bfe1a595477db6826bd2126c63ac2091efb7ec76347a8e7f81ba17e3de6c.png",
            "link": "https://seekingalpha.com/news/4674421-yelp-announces-workforce-reduction-affecting-nearly-5-percent-of-employees",
            "pub_date": "2026-11-19 05:33:52",
            "source": "seekalpha",
            "kind": 1,
            "language": "en"
        },
